  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Why is the grade different from SSL Labs?",
      "a": "This tool only reports observations and does not align with the SSL Labs score. SSLv2/SSLv3, EXPORT suites and active vulnerability probes are out of scope; they are called out on the page instead of being silently omitted."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is the handshake simulation identical to a real browser?",
      "a": "No. It performs handshakes using each client's parameter profile (version range, suites, ALPN). The result answers \"can a client with these parameters connect\", not a byte-level ClientHello replay."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why does something say \"not measurable\"?",
      "a": "OCSP stapling and session resumption state are not exposed by the upstream TLS library yet. They do not take part in scoring and are never reported as unsupported."
    },
    {
      "q": "What happens with internal addresses?",
      "a": "The egress guard blocks private, loopback and link-local addresses and returns `SSRF_BLOCKED`."
    },
    {
      "q": "How long does a full scan take?",
      "a": "Roughly 50 handshakes plus 5 outbound requests, typically 15-40 seconds; slow sites can approach the 2-minute budget. Select only the checks you need."
    }
  ]
